Welcome to HoverWare, a set of libraries and applications designed to
help the poor demo writers of the world.  The directory structure
of HoverWare is as follows:

	README		This file
	bin/		HoverWare executable programs:
	    gfx2hw		Convert GraphEd-style objects to HoverWare
	    spinner		Play HoverWare animations
	examples/	HoverWare sample files:
	    README		A description of the sample files
	include/	Header files for building HoverWare programs
	    hw.h		Always include this in your .c files
	    hw_os.h		Included by hw.h
	    hw_types.h		Included by hw.h
	    hw_protos.h		Included by hw.h
	    hw_strings.h	Included by hw.h
	lib/		HoverWare program libraries:
	    libhwnull.a         A HoverWare library with no display
				capability; useful for creating
				utilities such as gfx2hw
	    libhwsb.a           A HoverWare library which uses the
				Starbase graphics API to render 3D
				graphics
	man/		HoverWare man pages
	    cat1/*.1		Documentation for executable programs
	    cat3/*.3		Documentation for functions and classes
	src/		HoverWare examples
	    spinner.c		Source from which spinner was built
	    Welcome.gfx		A simple HoverWare animation
	    box.gfx		A box, used by Welcome.gfx
	    Text.gfx		The text "HoverWare!", used by Welcome.gfx
	    Texture/		Textures used by the Welcome demo
		Earth			A texture of the Earth's surface
		Jupiter			A texture of Jupiter's clouds

For more information about HoverWare, consult the man/cat3/hw.3 man page
as a starting place.  HoverWare will run on HP-UX 10.20 systems or later.
To run the spinner program on the provided demo, do the following:

	cd src
	../bin/spinner -rgb Welcome.gfx

If you have hardware-accelerated texture mapping (Visualize-48 with optional
texture memory), you may omit the -rgb argument.  Or, if you want to run
slowly, leave it in...
